bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    engine2d_retained_damage_replay_differs_from_full_frame_on_vulkan_embedded_surfaces_2026-11-26, 0, "On Vulkan the full frame renders every embedded-surface batch (including opaque clipped WM window chrome) through its own offscreen layer and composites it, while _engine2d_draw_ir_render_composition_damaged_with_images drew the same batch directly onto the parent under the damage clip; translucent pixels (window shadow) round differently, so a retained replay that touches a window is not equal to the full frame."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    engine2d_retained_damage_replay_differs_from_full_frame_on_vulkan_embedded_surfaces_2026-11-26, P2, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "retained damage replay differs from the full frame on Vulkan embedded surfaces", doc/08_tracking/bug/engine2d_retained_damage_replay_differs_from_full_frame_on_vulkan_embedded_surfaces_2026-11-26.md, 1, test/02_integration/rendering/engine2d_wm_local_lane_clock_tick_spec.spl, 2026-11-26, 2026-11-26, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    engine2d_retained_damage_replay_differs_from_full_frame_on_vulkan_embedded_surfaces_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-26 wm-lane-20261126 Linux aarch64 seed fb80903917d6d5f5: hosted local-lane clock tick, focused 140x84 window at (10,36), default chrome; forced full device readback of the replay vs a fresh Vulkan executor frame of the new tick: 240 px differ at x 150..154 y>=72 (e.g. 4280638921 vs 4280639178) on NVIDIA GB10 and llvmpipe. Fix: replay layers exactly the batches the full frame layers (one layer per batch per replay, composited under each clip); the same spec then passes on GB10."
    engine2d_retained_damage_replay_differs_from_full_frame_on_vulkan_embedded_surfaces_2026-11-26, 1, "2026-11-27 Fable review fixes: one shared layering predicate (_engine2d_draw_ir_uses_embedded_surface) for full frame and replay; replay is batch-major over disjoint damage rects and acquires each layer like the full frame (single-slot pool off Vulkan, for the non-reclaiming SimpleOS bump heap); spec canary poison proven visible through engine before the read; themed spec keeps CPU parity in the clock box except the tracked corner-AA pixels (<=20, which equal the fresh device frame). On 89f2b4e1854, seed fb80903917d6d5f5: group-opacity 2/2 and themed 8/8 on NVIDIA GB10 and llvmpipe. Perf: any replay touching a window costs about a full frame on Vulkan (layer create/render/readback)."
